<h1>Terms</h1>
<p class="lede">Read this before relying on any number on this site.</p>

<h2>Theoretical estimates only</h2>
<p>All weights produced by this calculator are <strong>theoretical (calculated)</strong> values derived from geometry and an assumed density. Actual pipe weight varies with manufacturing tolerance, wall-thickness tolerance, coatings, and end finish. Always verify against mill certificates or physical weighing where it matters.</p>

<h2>Not engineering advice</h2>
<p>This tool does not replace engineering design. Do not use it — or any number on this site — for pressure design, lifting calculations, support/structural calculations, or safety-critical decisions. Consult a qualified engineer.</p>

<h2>Dimension data</h2>
<p>Schedule dimensions are cross-checked reference data with documented verification levels (see <a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a>). They are not a substitute for the official ASME standard text. For critical applications, confirm dimensions against the current edition of the applicable standard.</p>

<h2>Sourcing assistance</h2>
<p>Any sourcing help is provided on a best-effort basis as described on the <a href="/about/">About</a> page. Quotations come from third-party suppliers and are labeled as such; we make no commitment on pricing, lead time, quality, or fulfillment.</p>

<h2>Acceptable use</h2>
<p>Do not abuse the calculator or any forms on this site (automated scraping, spam, or hostile input). We may rate-limit or block abusive traffic.</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>These terms may be updated as the site evolves. Material changes will be noted here with a revision date.</p>
<p><em>Last revised: 2026-10-06.</em></p>
</Layout>
